  "opencli": "0.1-draft",
  "info": {
    "title": "aexp: verified-lesson memory for any agent (AgentExperience.NET, preview).",
    "version": "0.1.0-preview.18",
    "description": "Preview, not production ready. The aexp command: verified-lesson memory for any agent, not only Microsoft Agent Framework ones. One .NET tool that is both a CLI (aexp run start/call/end, finalize, recall, lessons, export, benefit) and an MCP stdio server (aexp mcp), over a local SQLite file by default or PostgreSQL. It drives the same library the MAF adapter uses: capture with sanitization, finalization against a verifier command the project's own config names, the Historical Reference block, recall by failure signature, the injection holdout, the lessons view and the measured export. It calls no model, never takes identity or scope from its arguments, and runs no command but the configured verifier. Install with dotnet tool install AgentExperience.Cli."
  },
